## Why This Is Asked
Tests end-to-end Snowflake-core pipeline design: ingestion, streams, tasks, late data handling, and anomaly scoring across accounts.

## Key Concepts
- Snowflake Streams, Tasks, external stages, MERGE, watermarking, rolling baselines, alerting.
- Data governance: access control, masking, retention.

## Code Example
```sql
-- Core objects (illustrative)
CREATE OR REPLACE STAGE RAW_EVENTS_STAGE URL='s3://region-lake/raw' FILE_FORMAT=(TYPE='JSON');
CREATE OR REPLACE TABLE RAW_EVENTS(
  event_id STRING, customer_id STRING, region STRING, amount NUMBER, ts TIMESTAMP_NTZ
);
CREATE OR REPLACE STREAM RAW_EVENTS_STREAM ON TABLE RAW_EVENTS (APPEND_ONLY = FALSE);
CREATE OR REPLACE TABLE FRAUD_SCORES(customer_id STRING, region STRING, date DATE, score FLOAT);
CREATE OR REPLACE TABLE FRAUD_WATERMARK(date DATE, max_ts TIMESTAMP_NTZ);
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you test late-arrival handling and boundary conditions?
- How would you scale the rolling baseline computation to thousands of regions and customers?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests cross‑account sharing, row filtering, masking, and auditable usage in Snowflake.

## Key Concepts
- Secure Data Sharing across accounts
- SECURE VIEWs with row-level access
- Masking policies for PII
- Query auditing via QUERY_HISTORY and usage logs
- Cost/complexity trade-offs in view-based filtering

## Code Example
```sql
-- Provider side (simplified)
CREATE SHARE SHARED_SALES;
GRANT USAGE ON DATABASE RAW TO SHARE SHARED_SALES;
GRANT SELECT ON ALL TABLES IN SCHEMA RAW.SALES TO SHARE SHARED_SALES;
ALTER SHARE SHARED_SALES ADD TABLE RAW.SALES;

-- Consumer side (simplified)
CREATE DATABASE SHARED_SALES_DB FROM SHARE PROVIDER.ACCOUNT.SHARED_SALES;

CREATE MASKING POLICY mp_customer_id AS (val STRING) RETURNS STRING ->
  CASE WHEN CURRENT_ROLE() = 'CONSUMER_ROLE' THEN 'REDACTED' ELSE val END;
ALTER TABLE RAW.SALES ALTER COLUMN customer_id SET MASKING POLICY mp_customer_id;

-- Region-aware view (region context assumed via session variable)
SET REGION_CONTEXT = 'NA';
CREATE OR REPLACE SECURE VIEW SHARED_SALES_DB.V_SALES_REGION_MASK AS
SELECT sale_id, amount, sale_ts, region, customer_id
FROM RAW.SALES
WHERE region = REGION_CONTEXT;
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you handle late region changes or region-specific data laws?
- What metrics would you collect to verify consumer usage against quotas?
